              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उपत्यका — upatyakā — \"a valley\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "upatyakā is built on upa, \"near, below\", with the suffix -tyaka; Pāṇini 5.2.34 forms it beside adhityakā, \"table-land\", from adhi, \"above\". MW glosses it \"land at the foot of a mountain, low-land\" and \"a valley\"."
            }
          ]
        },
